Whether what you're doing is correct is not generally something I'm able to answer without looking at the data in detail, which I generally wouldn't have time to do

What methods you should use for QTL analysis is not something that can be answered in this forum. Take a look at the tutorials at http://rqtl.org/tutorials, or the R/qtl book (see http://rqtl.org/book).

I don't see how summary.fitqtl() could produce the four columns you provided.

karl

