I found that only use a set of markers, which is 7000 out of 30,000 SNPs, actually lead to inaccurate confidence intervals of my final QTLs, though the QTL location are more or less similar. But due to the limit memory, I can't run the scantwo permutation for 30,000 markers (scantwopermhk also not work with such huge amount of markers).

So my question is: can I use the permutation result from 7000 markers for the stepwiseqtl scan with 30,000 markers? The individual number and the phenotype values are exactly the same for the scantwo permutation and the stepwiseqtl.

Thanks!

