Dear Dr Karl

I have scanned QTLs on 21 chromosomes of a Doubled Haploid wheat using scanone and i only get low LODs (attached file). I used the codes below. I used "threshold = 1" because at 3 I could not get any LOD peaks.

So, will it be possible for me to continue with these results and get QTLs?

#QTL analysis with estimated genetic map
> SNP1 <- calc.genoprob(SNP1, step = 2, off.end = 0.0, error.prob = 0.01, map.function = "kosambi", stepwidth = "fixed")
> SNP1 <- sim.geno(SNP1, step = 2, n.draws = 16, off.end = 0.0, error.prob = 0.01, map.function = "kosambi", stepwidth = "fixed")

> #Scanning without permutation
> out.hk <http://out.hk> <- scanone(SNP1, pheno.col = 2:21, model = "normal", method = "hk")
> print(summary(out.hk <http://out.hk>), force = TRUE)
> summary(out.hk <http://out.hk>, threshold = 1, format = "allpeaks")

